        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Ancient Egyptian religion</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 3100 BCE – c. 537 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Origin</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley, with prehistoric roots; shaped with the first kings around 3100 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founder or early teachers</span><span class="info-stat-val">None: it grew from the cults of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>’s towns and kings; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhenaten">Akhenaten</a> briefly imposed the worship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aten">Aten</a> in the 14th century BCE</span></div>
